From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Victor Fuentes <victor@vlinkz.dev>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 08:36:37 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] remoteproc: qcom: sysmon: Skip the state query without a
 shutdown-ack IRQ

The interrupt is optional, and querying a negative IRQ warns on every
late attach of such a subsystem.

Fixes: 16472c99f469 ("remoteproc: qcom: pas: Add late attach support for subsystems")

Signed-off-by: Victor Fuentes <victor@vlinkz.dev>
---
 drivers/remoteproc/qcom_sysmon.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_sysmon.c b/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_sysmon.c
index 61e1038328e8..54a6b25201f0 100644
--- a/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_sysmon.c
+++ b/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_sysmon.c
@@ -739,7 +739,7 @@ bool qcom_sysmon_shutdown_irq_state(struct qcom_sysmon *sysmon)
 	bool shutdown_state;
 	int ret;
 
-	if (!sysmon)
+	if (!sysmon || sysmon->shutdown_irq <= 0)
 		return false;
 
 	ret = irq_get_irqchip_state(sysmon->shutdown_irq,
-- 
2.43.0

